WEBVTT

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.120
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.230
<b>Teshima
 
Aoyagi</b>

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:32.980
<b>Teshima
Koga
Aoyagi</b>

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.910
<i>RIDE.15 Koga's Goal</i>

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.280
Junta!

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.580
<i>You won. You won, Junta.</i>

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.060
<b>Victory</b>

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.690
<i>You worked so hard.</i>

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.350
<i>That must've been difficult, Junta.</i>

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.130
<i>My wishes and support 
didn't help you one bit.</i>

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.320
<i>It was all your strength.</i>

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.420
<i>You did it all on your own.</i>

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.340
<i>Congratulations, Junta.</i>

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.220
I knew you were coming right away.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.210
That's a convenient device.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.690
Junta.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.320
Sorry. I'm taking a break.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.730
A break?

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:20.700
You said your legs and back were 
cramping and brought me down with you.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.950
Your leg cramped up first.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.780
M-My legs didn't cramp!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.170
I'm the one they call the Stamina Simpleton!

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.010
You're the one who lost his 
balance first, Kimitaka!

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.340
No, it was you, Junta!

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.230
No, you!

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.220
No, you!

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.800
It doesn't matter who it was.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.680
You're right, Aoyagi.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.180
You're right. It doesn't matter.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:48.660
It's been a while since 
we spoke face to face.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.900
Our first-year Inter-High was the last time.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:57.780
But I'm glad I gave everything I had then.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.200
Given the team's situation, I was 
the only one who could go for it.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.910
Even when I had it to do over, 
I think I would still do it.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.900
I gave everything I had in that race.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.740
What happened was unfortunate, 
but I don't regret it.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.540
<i>Kimitaka...</i>

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.820
It's frustrating, but it can't be helped.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.210
Let's ride.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.210
What?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.600
Isn't this a training camp?

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.490
There's still something I have to 
do before my three years are up.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.310
I'm a man of only 980 kilometers.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.710
So I must complete one thousand kilometers.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.720
Good work, Koga-san. That was amazing.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.160
During last year's Inter-High,

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.950
thanks for staying behind for us 
and supporting Sohoku High School.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.700
I'll be going this year, Onoda.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.450
I'll support the team with all my might.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.410
Thank you.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:51.940
Imaizumi...

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.500
You're a second-year ace,
just like Kinjou-san was back then.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.880
Don't waver. Attack.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.280
We'll be counting on you near the finish line.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.260
Yes, sir.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.550
Naruko...

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.500
Looks like you're working on something 
new to surprise us again this year.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.220
It'll be a piece of cake.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.270
I'll be heating things up 
this summer to 300 degrees!

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.900
Don't burn yourself to death.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.240
Kaburagi, are you feeling uneasy?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.090
You're the only first-year.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.740
I was the only one, too.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.020
Give everything you've got.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:33.190
It's the only way you'll be 
able to see the next step.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:34.920
Yes, sir.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.840
Don't be too unreasonable, Kimitaka.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.680
And you guys... I don't have 
to tell you what to do.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.680
I know how hard you've worked until now.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.280
One last thing. Get injured.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.640
What?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.980
And then I'll ride in the Inter-High for you!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.720
No way.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.100
Does that mean you'll replace us
 if we let our guard down?

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.800
We'll be careful.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:06.160
<i>Do your best. Don't get hurt.</i>

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:13.290
<i>It's all right. You can come 
to me for advice anytime.</i>

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.850
<i>I know a lot about injuries.</i>

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.570
Here we go.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.730
I'm sorry, but the five-kilometer
course is reserved.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.350
<b>Reserved</b>

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.350
Well, that's a shock.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.340
I heard this place was famous.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.110
I took the train and a taxi to get here.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.060
There's actually a high school bicycle 
club holding a training camp here.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.820
They're here for four days until tomorrow.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.410
<i>Imaizumi-kun and Naruko-kun are fast.</i>

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.620
<i>Their speed is incredible, 
and their cornering is fast.</i>

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.040
<i>And they've gotten even stronger 
at this training camp.</i>

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.340
<i>They're riding right on the edge.</i>

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.730
You're so annoying.
Stop getting ahead on corners.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.800
Are you stupid?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.810
It's your fault for riding so slowly 
that I'm overtaking you on them.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.180
You're not overtaking me. 
I'm letting you pass me.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.730
<i>I'm short of breath,
and I'm barely keeping up.</i>

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.310
<i>But they're conversing normally.</i>

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.230
Hotshot, you take it easy.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.440
I'll definitely win.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.820
I'll pay the price.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.100
I'm always riding right on the edge.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.880
Sorry, but that's how I'm prepared to ride.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.350
<i>The price?</i>

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.490
<i>What price?</i>

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:38.210
<i>He's certainly gotten stronger and better.</i>

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.460
<i>Naruko-kun must have something up his sleeve.</i>

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.880
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.480
<i>A promise is a promise.</i>

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.010
<i>I quit being a sprinter, 
but I have a good goal now.</i>

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:57.200
<i>I hate doing as that hotshot said,
but I'll do whatever it takes.</i>

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.140
<i>I'll become stronger and stronger.</i>

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:06.400
<i>I'll make Idiotsuji admit defeat 
and reclaim the title of sprinter!</i>

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:11.610
<i>I'll even practice climbing 
to achieve my goal!</i>

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.630
He's fast. He's accelerating!

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.120
Naruko-kun's accelerating on a climb!

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.040
That idiot.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.780
<i>Until then, I'll abandon them.</i>

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.310
<i>That's the price I'll pay.</i>

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.090
In that case...

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.340
Could we at least take a look at the track?

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.250
Sure.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:36.720
<i>They asked me not to let anyone in,
but since these two came from so far away...</i>

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.500
Fight!

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.480
Good work.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:47.630
What?

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.830
What is this fun and games cycling event?

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.860
This is a training camp?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.620
Gross.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.480
I came to see how they were doing 
since they're the champions.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.420
But all they have are more members now.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.500
Are they sure they weren't 
stronger last year?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.340
He's no good.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.800
He's weak, too.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.800
This one's not so bad.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.220
But since he's not wearing a yellow jersey, 
does that mean he's not a regular?

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.610
Hey, it's rooster head. 
The rooster head's here.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.980
So he hasn't quit. He's still riding.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.840
Riding hard, too.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.550
I don't know what he's riding for, though.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:36.870
Is that tall guy behind them their ace?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:40.910
That's right. That's Caterpillizumi-kun,

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.210
who hasn't learned to fly yet.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.030
It's hard to tell from so far away.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.300
I wish we could get closer.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.870
Ideally, I'd like to feel 
his muscles for myself.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.570
It's getting cloudy.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.680
It might rain.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.140
I should get some rain gear.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.080
Maybe I'll take some for 
Naruko-kun and the others.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.400
Hello.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.240
Who are you?

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:17.720
My name is Komari.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.240
I'm interested in a few things.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.050
Could I ask you some questions?

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.090
<i>What?</i>

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.170
<i>He disappeared.</i>

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.520
<i>Komari...</i>

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:41.140
<i>I see. He left...</i>

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.650
To meet them face to face.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:50.060
That guy has no restraint.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.900
What? Uh, Komari-kun?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.860
That's right. I'm a first-year.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.780
I'm looking for him so I can touch him.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.580
Could you tell me all about...

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.260
Your ace, Imaizumi-san?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.640
Oh, Komari-kun.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.710
Yeah, right. Komari-kun.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:21.710
I know you. I asked who you were 
because you showed up so suddenly.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:24.360
You're the new student, uh...

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:29.700
Komori-kun, right? I remember you.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:31.020
<b><i>Maximum Eloquence
Senior Smile</i></b>

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.380
<i>Has this first-year always been on the team?</i>

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.910
<i>We have a lot of new students this year.</i>

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:40.990
<i>I'm not good at remembering faces,
but Naruko-kun said...</i>

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.540
Everyone looks up to you, Onoda-kun.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.680
You should remember the faces 
and names of the first-years.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.620
They'd be disappointed if they 
knew you didn't recognize them.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:53.630
<i>I'll use this opportunity to 
close the distance between us.</i>

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.160
<i>He thinks I'm one of Sohoku 
High School's first-years.</i>

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.340
<i>He must be a second or third-year.</i>

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.140
<i>I don't feel any pressure from him.</i>

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.820
Ahem. Komori-kun...

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.040
<i>Okay, here we go.</i>

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:12.020
<i>Time for Makishima-san's
Stimulating Conversation Skills!</i>

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:12.770
What...

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:15.040
What do you do for fun?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:15.970
Wash my hands.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:17.590
The sky sure is blue.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.050
It's raining.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.110
<i>This isn't stimulating at all!</i>

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.160
Is your ace Imaizumi-san strong?

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.410
Or is he weak?

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.720
What? Weak?

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:34.050
No way. He's strong.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.880
He's fast. Can't you tell by watching him?

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.840
He's always calm. He's a good guy 
and easy to get along with.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.430
Is he stronger than Midousuji-san?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.680
What?

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.820
Not Naruko-kun?

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.150
Wh-Why would you ask about Midousuji-kun?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.400
Which is it?

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.270
I'm not sure.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:07.410
From my perspective, they're equally amazing,
and they're both good people.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:09.410
<i>Good people?</i>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.830
This is just my opinion, but...

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:18.170
I don't think it matters if 
one is better than the other.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:27.050
Are you rejecting bicycle racing itself?

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:31.360
Once they start riding, their relative 
strength and weakness becomes clear.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.930
That's how road racing works.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:35.310
Am I wrong?

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.710
I'm not sure how to put it.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.820
I think you'll understand 
once you start riding.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:46.570
But I don't think that's all there is to it.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:50.540
<i>What a strange person. Once I start riding?</i>

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.590
<i>He's the one who's never ridden before.</i>

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.170
<i>That's all racing is.</i>

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:01.170
<i>I spoke to him because he's wearing a 
yellow jersey, but he must be a sub.</i>

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.040
Oh, sorry, Komori-kun.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:07.470
I came to get rain gear.
I'm heading back to the track.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:09.010
How disappointing.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.090
<i>Since he was wearing glasses,</i>

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:18.810
<i>I thought he was last year's
Inter-High champion, Onoda Sakamichi...</i>

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.700
<i>What kind of muscles are these?</i>

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.210
<i>They're good!</i>

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:42.250
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.960
My cleats slipped...

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.630
<i>I almost made a noise.</i>

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:53.970
<i>They're so flexible and springy.</i>

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:58.230
<i>This guy must be...</i>

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.600
Onoda-san...

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.520
Huh? What?

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.990
<i>Last year's champion, Onoda Sakamichi!</i>

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.700
<i>Let me... Let me touch you again.</i>

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.560
<i>Let me see!</i>

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.380
What are you doing?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.830
You're not from our team.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:21.600
What?

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.790
No, I'm just visiting.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:29.450
I'm Kyoto Fushimi High School 
first-year Kishigami Komari.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.930
What?

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.680
I'm a simple masseuse.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.040
Don't glare at me like that.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.180
What's Kyoto Fushimi High School doing here?

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.310
It looked like rain,
so I came here to stay dry.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:47.220
I'm Sohoku High School third-year Koga.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.030
If you have business with us,
you can speak to me.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.530
I was mostly finished anyway.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:55.580
Don't worry about it. I'll leave.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.770
There's another one of you up there.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.380
Both of you, get out of here.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:08.120
I'm excited for this summer, Koga-senpai.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.060
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:16.310
Since you're wearing that jersey,
you won't be riding in this summer's race.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.420
It looks like the rain's letting up.
I'll be leaving now.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:29.920
How did it go?

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.790
It had me panting.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:37.160
I nearly said something twice!

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.210
Two riders are coming.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.840
Who will it be?

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.960
Idiot!

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:50.670
You can't be serious!

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.560
All right!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.230
Naruko-san finished a 
thousand kilometers first!

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:10.340
How did he pull ahead at the finish line?

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:12.400
<i>Naruko-kun is evolving.</i>

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:16.870
<i>He was going way faster 
than before at the end.</i>

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:23.160
<i>I'm still nowhere close to as good 
as Naruko-kun and Imaizumi-kun.</i>

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.410
<i>I have to get stronger, too.</i>

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:28.890
Hey, idiot. I won.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.940
Shut up. Don't celebrate so much 
just because you happened to win.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.200
Naruko-san, here's a towel andー

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:37.200
Nah.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:43.020
Boy, I'm thirsty. Maybe I'll 
have Imaizumi-kun go get mine.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.150
Just like he promised.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.180
Hotshot, we're almost on our final lap.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.910
How do you feel about second place doing

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:56.440
whatever the first to finish a 
thousand kilometers says for a day?

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:58.580
Fine.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.030
Here.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.430
Ow!

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.850
What was that for?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.390
My hand slipped.

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:08.580
I heard you say, "Here!"

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.340
Yeah, but the sweat...

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:10.960
What are they, kids?

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.080
Oh, right, Onoda.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:18.140
When there's a crosswind,
ride one wheel closer downwind.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:18.640
Okay.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:22.270
Usually, you ride directly behind 
the wheel to avoid the wind,

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.500
but in the case of a crosswind,

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:27.060
you'll be blown by less wind 
by riding slightly ahead.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:31.660
You're a climber. Your ability 
to reduce how much energy

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.740
you spend on flats affects 
your team's performance.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.500
During this training camp and our 
practices until the Inter-High,

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.410
I'll teach you everything 
I know about racing.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.370
Focus while you ride.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.240
Yes, sir.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:45.660
Kaburagi-kun!

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.810
You caught up?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:53.460
Imaizumi-san and Naruko-san 
beat me, and now you, too?

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.610
Damn it.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:59.350
Kaburagi's struggling.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:03.010
His body's not moving the way he wants.

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:07.520
Of course it isn't.
This course has steep slopes.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:12.020
He hasn't realized it yet,
but once he does, he'll get faster.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:17.450
Kaburagi Issa is definitely a sprinter.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:22.510
<i>I can go fast on the flats, so why?</i>

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:26.330
<i>I should be able to climb faster 
if I pedal the same way.</i>

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.750
A sprinter? Kaburagi-kun?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:34.100
Aoyagi said he might surpass Tadokoro-san 
by the time he's a third-year,

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.380
if he trains hard.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.360
Th-That's amazing.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.340
But you're not going to tell Kaburagi-kun?

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.230
I thought he'd notice after 
riding a thousand kilometers.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:47.680
He's either a total idiot or a genius.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.060
<b>Aoyagi</b>

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.440
Hime!

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.060
<i>I managed to pass Teshima-san.</i>

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:03.740
<i>There must be some way to go faster.</i>

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:06.580
Spri...

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:11.340
<i>Spring, like the season.</i>

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:15.140
<i>How can I go faster?</i>

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:17.180
He's coming!

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.760
You can do it, Koga-san!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.180
<i>Almost there.</i>

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:24.600
<i>Kinjou-san,</i>

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.350
<i>it took me a while, but I...</i>

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.730
<i>...finally completed the
 thousand-kilometer training camp.</i>

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.340
Good work, Kimitaka.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.280
That was a long thousand kilometers.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.650
I know.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.410
It took me three years.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.950
That doesn't change the fact that you did it.

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:53.170
<b>Koga
Sugimoto</b>

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:57.280
The Sohoku High School 
training camp is now over!

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.180
Thank you, sir!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.220
Good morning.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.300
How'd the training camp go?

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.880
I won.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.220
By a millimeter.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.330
Good work, guys.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.850
Now, it's time for one last push.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:16.480
<b>Bicycle Racing Club Training Camp
 Makeup Classes
 Period 1 7:30 – 8:20
 Period 2 8:30 – 9:20
 Period 3 9:30 – 10:20
 Period 4 10:30 – 11:20
 Period 5 11:30 – 12:20</b>

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.480
At your makeup classes.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.980
I-I forgot!

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.950
<i>My second Inter-High...</i>

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.120
<i>Let's do this.</i>

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.950
<i>I'll destroy all the competition.</i>

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:32.870
<i>We're a six-man team.</i>

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:37.090
<i>Push aside the pressure and reach the top.</i>

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:43.720
<i>Am I not an all-rounder?</i>

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.350
That can't be right.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.280
<i>Will you...</i>

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.850
<i>Will you be watching from 
far away, Makishima-san?</i>

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:02.460
<i>Honestly, I feel anxious about riding 
in the Inter-High without you.</i>

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:09.980
<i>But I'll ride as hard as I can so I 
can deliver the best possible news.</i>

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:26.070
He is very fast. Green Japanese boy...

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:29.970
Teshima made it at the training camp.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:32.930
The Inter-High is starting soon.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:36.820
If I don't go to show my support...

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.920
They'll probably yell at me.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:17.840
Ready, start.

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:23.540
I'm the fastest.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.260
That one doesn't count. Reset, reset.

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:27.490
One more time.

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:28.770
No way.

00:23:28.770 --> 00:23:30.130
It'll always turn out the same.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:33.740
G-Guys, maybe we should stop.

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:36.890
<i>My stomach!</i>

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE  The Second Inter-High</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:51.000
<b><i>The high cadence
 continues!!</i></b>
